# Call-site ledger of pyflakes at 5324946c5d8602697f5df6d98ad162920b3e5d61 (4.1.0).
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md; pyflakes.md
# shows how this ledger applies them and records each judgement. The package
# supports Python 3.11 and later (setup.py: python_requires='>=3.11'); the
# branches for 3.12 to 3.15 run. The checker dispatches on ast node classes by
# name (getNodeHandler) and runs deferred callables (_run_deferred): see
# pyflakes.md, "Node dispatch" and "Deferred functions".
default reject pyflakes.checker.VariableKey.__eq__: no VariableKey is compared, hashed as a dict key or set element, or searched for at this site; VariableKey objects are made only by convert_to_value (checker.py:201), which only Checker.DICT calls; they are in its local lists keys and values and the Counters made from them (the DICT sites accept the candidate), and a VariableKey inside a tuple key also reaches the message_args of MultiValueRepeatedKeyLiteral (checker.py:1837), where it is formatted with %r (object.__repr__) and never compared
default reject pyflakes.checker.VariableKey.__hash__: no VariableKey is hashed at this site (dict key, set element, subscript key); VariableKey objects are made only by convert_to_value (checker.py:201), which only Checker.DICT calls, and only the Counters of DICT hash them (those sites accept the candidate); a VariableKey inside a tuple key also reaches the message_args of MultiValueRepeatedKeyLiteral (checker.py:1837), where nothing hashes it
default reject pyflakes.checker.Binding.__repr__, pyflakes.checker.Builtin.__repr__, pyflakes.checker.Scope.__repr__, pyflakes.messages.Message.__str__: no f-string placeholder or %-operand at this site is a binding, a scope or a message; the formatted values are str (names, module names, file names, error texts, the result of dict.__repr__), int or a class (each explicit site decides these candidates itself)

